    "done_when": "When a promoted run's manifest carries a landing: line, reckon/crew/promotion.py writes it as a comment on the node's plan section through the versioned write (_store.read_plan and write_plan with the VersionConflict retry that _record_landing_comment already uses), bumping the plan's version, and never relies on a git merge of the plan HTML for that record. A run whose manifest has no landing: line keeps today's behaviour, including the worker-authored deferral in _worker_authored_landing_record, because workers only start writing landing: lines when the plan's section 2 changes the prompt. tests/test_promotion_writes_the_landing_line.py synthesises a repository and passes at exit 0 with three cases: a landing: line lands as a comment with the plan version bumped; a run without one is unchanged; a concurrent plan edit between read and write is retried, not lost. tests/test_landing_comment_authorship.py passes. The manifest cites the reuse map at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/s25-coord/s25-reuse-map-record-and-promotion/reuse-map.md for promotion.py _record_landing_comment and _worker_authored_landing_record. The declared negative control is applied, the landing-line case is observed to leave no comment, and that log's absolute path is in the manifest.",
